Start Description            : 1. Telnet to RG
#                               : 2. Load the required BGW320 image
#                               : 3. Go to the linux prompt
#                               : 4. The default value of Critical rise threshold is 80 and maximum value is 100 and when set the Critical rise threshold value less than 3 then CPU will reach to critical state.
#                               : 5. Execute the below ba-cli command for reaching to critical state
#                               :    ba-cli Device.DeviceInfo.ProcessStatus.CPU.1.CriticalRiseThreshold=2
#                               :    ba-cli Device.DeviceInfo.ProcessStatus.CPU.?
#                               : 6. Verify after reaching to critical state, time stamp should be updated properly in below shown parameter.
#                               :    ba-cli Device.DeviceInfo.ProcessStatus.CPU.1.CriticalRiseTimeStamp?
#                               :    ba-cli Device.DeviceInfo.ProcessStatus.CPU.?
#                               : 7. Verify the pidstat log file generated once the critical state is reached
#                               :    cd /var/run/
#                               :    ls
#                               :    cat /var/run/rm_pidstat_full.txt
#                               : 8. After running the above commands in linux prompt log file is generated.
#                               : 9. Restart the RG
#                               : 10. Once RG is up and running check the Pidstat log
